.TITLE "defaults"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Accesses the macOS user defaults system. It allows you to read, write, and delete preferences for applications and system services from the command line.

.DIV "TLDR"
**defaults read domain**
Reads all the preferences for a specific application domain.
> __read__ read command | __domain__ application identifier

**defaults write domain key value**
Writes a new preference setting for a specific application.
> __write__ write command | __domain__ application identifier | __key__ preference name | __value__ setting value

**defaults delete domain key**
Removes a specific preference setting from a domain.
> __delete__ removal command | __domain__ application identifier | __key__ preference name

**defaults find query**
Searches through all preference domains for a specific string.
> __find__ search command | __query__ search term

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Many system changes made with __defaults write__ require a restart of the affected application or service (like the __Finder__ or __Dock__) to take effect.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"

